*** PROJECT: BUILDING A VALUE-WEIGHTED INDEX

This project designs and implements a market-value (cap)–weighted equity index to track aggregate stock performance across sectors. Using NYSE listing data, we (1) import and clean company fundamentals, (2) filter to firms with valid sector tags, and (3) normalize market capitalization (USD mm). We then select index constituents by choosing the largest company in each sector, retrieve matching historical price series, and compute per-period index weights as capᵢ / Σcap. The index level is constructed across time using weighted returns, enabling transparent attribution where larger companies drive proportionally larger moves—consistent with major benchmarks (e.g., S&P 500, NASDAQ Composite).
Deliverables include: reproducible data pipelines (read_excel/read_csv), a validated constituent list with names, caps, and last prices, the time-series index, and comparative performance views. Outcome: a robust, sector-balanced, cap-weighted index suitable for monitoring, backtesting, and portfolio benchmarking.

